Vulkanstorm licence
===================

Vulkanstorm is dual-licensed. You may use, modify and distribute it under
either of these two licences, at your choice:

  * the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
    (LICENSE-LGPL-2.1; in binary packages, LGPL-license.txt), or
  * the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any
    later version (LICENSE-GPL-3.0; in binary packages,
    GPL-3.0-license.txt).

The exact terms differ by origin:

  * Code from Linden Lab and the Phoenix Firestorm Project, and Rust ports
    of that code:
        SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only OR GPL-3.0-or-later
    Linden Lab and Firestorm release this code under LGPL-2.1 only. Section
    3 of LGPL-2.1 lets any licensee apply the ordinary GNU GPL, version 2 or
    any newer version, to a copy instead; Vulkanstorm offers that option
    with GPL version 3 or later.
  * Original Vulkanstorm code:
        SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later OR GPL-3.0-or-later
  * Third-party components keep their own licences.

Binary packages: the viewer binaries currently built from this tree link
OpenSSL 1.1.1, whose licence is not compatible with GPL-3.0
(doc/licensing.md, "Open points"). Until it is replaced, the GPL-3.0
option applies to the source code only, and the binaries are offered under
LGPL-2.1.

NOTICE.md explains which files belong to which group, how to choose a
licence, and links the audit of the libraries the viewer links with
(doc/licensing.md).

Copyright notices in the source files remain in force. Linden Lab and
Firestorm copyright notices and licence headers are kept unchanged: the
LGPL-2.1-only terms they state are one of the two options above.

Source code: https://github.com/anne-skydancer/vulkanstorm
